# LeakSanitizer suppressions for process-global allocations made by third-party
# runtime libraries. These are initialised once per process and never released,
# which LSan reports as leaks when the test binary exits:
#
#   - the proprietary NVIDIA GL driver keeps per-process dispatch state alive
#     even after every EGL surface and context has been destroyed;
#   - libmpv registers with the session D-Bus on first use and leaves the bus
#     connection to process teardown.
#
# Leaks in our own code are still reported: nothing below matches a frame from
# this repository.
leak:libnvidia-glsi
leak:libnvidia-glcore
leak:libGLX_nvidia
leak:libEGL_nvidia
leak:libdbus-1
